WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.517
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Bunny Breaths.

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:21.034
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:21.034 --> 00:00:24.944
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:24.944 --> 00:00:28.854
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:28.854 --> 00:00:37.977
This is a breathing practice with a bunny shape. Bunnies breathe in little sniffs. We will borrow that: three small sniffs in through your nose, then one long, slow breath out.

00:00:37.977 --> 00:00:48.404
The sniffs are tiny — sniff, sniff, sniff — like a bunny checking the garden air. Small and gentle. Never big gasps. Your hands stay resting on your desk the whole time.

00:00:48.404 --> 00:01:00.134
Then the breath out is long and easy, like a soft breeze. Sniff in small. Breathe out long. The pattern is a guide — a round with two sniffs is a complete practice, too.

00:01:00.134 --> 00:01:05.347
Nothing is ever held. The air moves in, the air moves out. That is the whole shape. Here we go.

00:01:05.347 --> 00:01:17.078
Round one. Sniff… sniff… sniff… and let it all out, long and slow.

00:01:17.078 --> 00:01:28.808
Round two. Sniff, sniff, sniff… and out, soft and easy.

00:01:28.808 --> 00:01:40.538
Round three. Sniff, sniff, sniff… and out. Let your shoulders drop as the long breath leaves.

00:01:40.538 --> 00:01:50.965
Round four. Sniff, sniff, sniff… and out, all the way.

00:01:50.965 --> 00:01:52.268
One last round, on your own count. Sniff in small… and breathe out long. Then let the pattern go, and just breathe the way your body wants to.

00:01:52.268 --> 00:02:03.998
Now hear the rules that keep this practice yours. The sniffs are gentle guides — they are never a test.

00:02:03.998 --> 00:02:15.728
If your sniffs are smaller, or there are only two, your practice is still complete. Your breath, your pace. And this is never a contest — not the longest, not the quietest, not the slowest, not the biggest.

00:02:15.728 --> 00:02:24.852
And if anything ever feels dizzy, or tight, or strange — if the sniffs ever feel like too much air — the move is simple: breathe normally. Normal breathing is always allowed, at any second. It is never a failure.

00:02:24.852 --> 00:02:26.155
Notice how your breathing feels now, all on its own. Nothing to fix. Nothing to hold.

00:02:26.155 --> 00:02:35.279
Sniff, sniff, sniff. One long breath out. Then let it be.

00:02:35.279 --> 00:02:41.796
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:41.796 --> 00:02:47.009
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:47.009 --> 00:02:53.526
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:53.526 --> 00:03:00.042
You're ready for what's next.
